---
// about.astro — full about page
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Mathim Divisions is a solo IT clarity practice — one human, supported by thoughtful tools, producing agency-level output."
>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 160px;">
    <p class="section-label">About the Practice</p>
    <h1 class="section-heading">One person. Clear work.</h1>
    <p class="section-subtitle">
      Mathim Divisions exists because small businesses deserve better IT support than
      they usually get — and better documentation than they usually see.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>The Practice</h2>
    <p>
      Mathim Divisions is a solo IT clarity practice run by Cassie, an IT technician
      with years of experience in managed services, documentation, and system administration.
      The practice focuses on three things: <strong>audits</strong> that show you what you
      actually have, <strong>documentation</strong> that people will actually read, and
      <strong>roadmaps</strong> that tell you what to do next and why.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most IT documentation is written for other IT people. Ours is written for the
      people who run the business — the office manager, the operations director, the
      person who just needs to know where the passwords are and whether the backups ran.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>How We Work</h2>
    <p>
      Every engagement starts with listening. We don't sell software, we don't push
      products, and we don't recommend solutions until we understand the problem.
      The deliverable is always a document you can hand to anyone — your next IT hire,
      your compliance auditor, or yourself six months from now when you need to remember
      how something works.
    </p>
    <p>
      Behind the scenes, the practice uses modern tools and automation to produce work
      at a level usually associated with larger firms. But the output is always human —
      clear, specific, and written for the people who will actually use it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>The Name</h2>
    <p>
      "Mathim" comes from childhood — a nonsense word that two friends invented as a
      pretend company name. Years later, Cassie asked permission to keep it. He said yes.
    </p>
    <p>
      "Divisions" is about clarity through separation. Taking a tangled IT environment
      and dividing it into coherent parts. Networks. Devices. Accounts. Backups. Policies.
      Each one clear on its own terms, with relationships mapped between them.
    </p>
    <p>
      It's not "Solutions." It's not "Systems." It's divisions — the act of making
      something complex into something you can see.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
